From 6ac85021bef7b5fde7721091462be4e804940775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/decode_audio: zero the padding of the input
 buffer

The input buffer has room for AV_INPUT_BUFFER_PADDING_SIZE bytes
after the data, but these bytes were never set to zero as the
documentation of that constant asks for. After the last frame of the
file they contained whatever was in the buffer before: stale data
from an earlier read or, for a file smaller than the buffer,
uninitialized stack memory.

decode_video.c clears the padding of its input buffer. Do the same
here whenever the buffer has been filled; the end of the data stays at
the same place until the next refill.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/decode_audio.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/examples/decode_audio.c b/doc/examples/decode_audio.c
index 2831c2f..46fb002 100644
--- a/doc/examples/decode_audio.c
+++ b/doc/examples/decode_audio.c
@@ -196,6 +196,9 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
     /* decode until eof */
     data      = inbuf;
     data_size = fread(inbuf, 1, AUDIO_INBUF_SIZE, f);
+    /* the padding after the end of the data has to be zeroed (this ensures
+     * that no overreading happens for damaged MPEG streams) */
+    memset(data + data_size, 0, AV_INPUT_BUFFER_PADDING_SIZE);
 
     while (data_size > 0) {
         ret = av_parser_parse2(parser, c, &pkt->data, &pkt->size,
@@ -218,6 +221,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
                         AUDIO_INBUF_SIZE - data_size, f);
             if (len > 0)
                 data_size += len;
+            memset(data + data_size, 0, AV_INPUT_BUFFER_PADDING_SIZE);
         }
     }
 
